From e53d5fba950d30a12edaaa31a0619902377a4663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:04:35 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] feat(desktop): Stations tab opens on all 212 stations

A user opened 1.3.0 looking for per-station results for the whole fleet
and found 45. The Stations tab opened on the held-out split and the
Overview only shows held-out stations, so the 167 training stations sat
behind a switch that was easy to miss.

- The Stations tab opens on "All". Name and fault-rate sorts run across
  both splits. Recall and false-alarm sorts keep held-out rows first,
  because in-sample model scores are optimistic (sortStationRows in
  data.ts).
- The count tiles follow the selected split, and a line under them says
  what they include. The subtitle and the sessions label also follow the
  split. Model evaluation (leaderboard, Overview) stays held-out only.
- Overview: the bundled-benchmark tile reads "Held-out stations", and
  both station cards say they are held-out only. "View all N stations"
  opens the Stations tab on every station with the search cleared. The
  research panel's "Station results" button keeps the chosen split.
- Builds without training rows (snapshot, ISO, web) render as before.

Fixed before commit, from review findings:
- "View all" kept a leftover search.
- The research CTA reset the chosen split.
- The fault-rate sort put held-out stations first.
- The Overview showed an unqualified 45.
- The Training-view subtitle claimed all 212 stations.
- One English plural was wrong.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
